              "login": "gemini-code-assist"
            },
            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request aims to normalize numeric strings with leading zeros for equivalence checks, which is a good improvement. However, the new helper function `_canonical_int_if_safe` introduces bugs when handling signed numbers (e.g., `+33` vs `33`, and `-0` vs `0`). I've provided a suggestion to fix these correctness issues by simplifying the implementation, which also makes it more robust.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe current implementation doesn't correctly normalize integers with signs. For example, `is_equiv('+33', '33')` and `is_equiv('-0', '0')` would both incorrectly return `False`.\n\nYou can simplify this function and fix these issues by converting the string to an `int` and back to a `str`. This will correctly handle all normalization cases: leading zeros, positive `+` signs, and signed zeros.\n\n```suggestion\n        return str(int(s))\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2025-07-10T00:44:27Z",
                  "databaseId": 2196264136,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -29,6 +29,18 @@ def compute_score(solution_str, ground_truth) -> float:\n \n \n # string normalization from https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/blob/master/lm_eval/tasks/hendrycks_math.py\n+import re\n+def _canonical_int_if_safe(s: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"\n+    If s is an integer (±digits), drop leading zeros; else return unchanged.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if re.fullmatch(r'[-+]?\\d+', s):\n+        sign = s[0] if s[0] in '+-' else ''\n+        num  = s[1:] if sign else s\n+        num  = num.lstrip('0') or '0'\n+        return sign + num",
                  "line": null,
                  "originalLine": 41,
                  "path": "verl/utils/reward_score/math.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2025-07-10T00:44:27Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/2446#discussion_r2196264136"
                }
              ],
              "pageInfo": {
